  data: {
    LLM: "Game: Block Dominoes. Double-six set (28 tiles). 2-4 players. Match tiles on train ends. Pass if can't play (no drawing). Doubles crosswise, NOT spinners. Two open ends only. Win by dominoing or lowest pips. Score difference. Game to 61 or 100.",
    Player: 'You have 5 tiles: 6-4, 6-3, 6-1, 3-2, 5-5. The open ends are 6 and 2. You control the 6-suit heavily. Do you play 6-4 to maintain your 6 presence on one end, or the 3-2 to keep all three 6-tiles? If the game blocks, your high pips hurt you.',
    objective: 'Be the first player to play all tiles from your hand, or have the lowest pip count in a blocked game.',
    gameplay: '1. **Start**: The player with the highest double (usually 6-6) plays first. 2. **Turn**: Each player in turn must place one tile that matches the pip value of an open end of the line. 3. **Doubles**: Doubles are played crosswise but are not spinners; they only provide two matching ends. 4. **Passing**: If you cannot play, you must pass your turn. 5. **End**: The round ends when a player is out of tiles or no player can make a move.',
    keyRules: [
      'The line always has exactly two open ends.',
      'No drawing from the boneyard during play.',
      'In a blocked game, the player with the lowest total pips wins the round.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: '2 to 4 players (4 players usually play in fixed partnerships).',
      deck: 'Standard double-six domino set consisting of 28 tiles.',
      equipment: 'One domino set, score sheet.',
      dealing: '2 players: 7 tiles each. 3 players: 5 tiles each. 4 players: 5 or 7 tiles each (depending on whether the boneyard is used). Remaining tiles are set aside face down.',
    },
    turnFlow: '1. **Start**: The player with the highest double (usually 6-6) plays first. 2. **Turn**: Each player in turn must place one tile that matches the pip value of an open end of the line. 3. **Doubles**: Doubles are played crosswise but are not spinners; they only provide two matching ends. 4. **Passing**: If you cannot play, you must pass your turn. 5. **End**: The round ends when a player is out of tiles or no player can make a move.',
    moveValidityConditions: {
      ante: 'Block Dominoes is a social matching game and does not utilize a monetary or chip-based ante system.',
      deal: 'The initial distribution of tiles to players is performed automatically by the system dealer at the start.',
      reveal_market: 'The boneyard remains face down and is not used during play; no public market of tiles exists.',
      buy_market: 'Players cannot purchase or swap tiles from any external area; they must play from their dealt hand.',
      buy_stock: 'Drawing from the boneyard is prohibited in the Block variant; players must pass if they cannot move.',
      fold: 'Participation is mandatory for every turn until a player goes domino or the game becomes blocked.',
      check: 'The game uses a matching structure rather than a vying structure where checking would be appropriate.',
      call: 'There is no pot or bet to match in Block Dominoes; competition is based on tile matching and pip counts.',
      bet: 'Progress is measured by point accumulation on a scorecard rather than through the wagering of chips.',
      raise: 'There are no wagering rounds in this game, so the value of the hand cannot be increased via raises.',
      declare: 'Results are determined by immediate physical tile matches; no separate declaration phase is required.',
      reveal_hand: "Hand tiles remain private until they are played onto the shared line during the player's turn.",
      award_pot: 'Winners are determined by cumulative game points rather than by awarding a physical pot of assets.',
      play_card: 'Block Dominoes is a tile-based game; card playing engine logic and rank hierarchies do not apply.',
      draw: 'Drawing from the stock is not part of the Block variant; hand replenishment does not occur.',
      discard: 'Tiles must be matched to the line to be removed from the hand; no separate discard pile is used.',
      pass: 'Allowed only when hand contains no tiles matching the line ends.',
      bid: 'The game does not use a bidding system to determine the dealer or game objectives.',
      meld: 'This is a line-matching game based on single tiles rather than creating sets or sequences in hand.',
      go_out: 'Going domino occurs automatically when the last tile is played; no separate engine action is needed.',
    },
    exampleHands: [
      'Opening deal: 2-4 player(s), 7 card(s) per player, 1 deck(s), initial visibility face_down.',
      'Opening flow: start in dealing; system may use deal_tiles before play_loop.',
      "Scoring check: Winner scores sum of losers' pips minus own pips. Game to 100 (2-player/partnership) or 61 (3-4 player). Expected outcome: 100.",
